---
import SidePage from '../../../layouts/SidePage.astro';
import BackendFacts from '../../../components/BackendFacts.astro';
import CheckLines from '../../../components/CheckLines.astro';
import { BACKEND_PAGES } from '../../../data/catalog.mjs';
import { backend } from '../../../lib/backends-table.mjs';
const b = backend('perplexity');
const page = BACKEND_PAGES.find((p) => p.slug === b.name);
---
<SidePage pages={BACKEND_PAGES} page={{ ...page, description: 'Perplexity Decisions through ThinkThen: address, model, key variable and check.' }} name="Backends">
  <h1>Perplexity Decisions</h1>
  <p class="lede">Select this backend with <code>--backend {b.name}</code>.</p>
  <BackendFacts name={b.name} />
  <p>Put your provider key in <code>{b.keys[0]}</code>. ThinkThen reads this variable when you select the backend.</p>
  <h2>Check the connection</h2>
  <p>Run <code>thinkthen check --backend {b.name} --timeout 90</code>. A preview with <code>--plan</code> needs no key and sends nothing.</p>
  <CheckLines name={b.name} />
  <p>Perplexity accepts one-sided yes-or-no criteria. Its Decisions route is distinct from the default System One route.</p>
  <p>The <a href="https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/decisions/quickstart">provider documentation</a> was checked on 2026-10-04. Read the provider's terms before sending sensitive text.</p>
  <h2>Price and limits</h2>
  <p>On 2026-10-04, <a href="https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/decisions/quickstart#pricing">Perplexity's published price</a> was $0.04 per million input tokens. Output tokens were free, with no per-request fee.</p>
  <p>The <a href="https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/decisions/quickstart#request-limits">published request limits</a> allow 128 questions, fewer than 262,144 input tokens and a body of at most 32 MiB. ThinkThen's own request limits still apply.</p>
  <h2>Pace requests</h2>
  <p>The backend paces nothing unless the configuration file sets <code>requests_per_minute</code>. Add <code>"perplexity": &#123;"requests_per_minute": 600&#125;</code> under <code>backends</code> to pace one process at ten requests a second.</p>
  <p>Perplexity's <a href="https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/decisions/quickstart#rate-limits">published organization limit</a> is ten requests a second. Multiple processes share that provider limit, while each ThinkThen process gets its own configured rate. Divide the allowance across processes when they run together. Perplexity also limits token bursts, so a request can reach a provider limit before the request rate does.</p>
  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/install/backends/">All backends</a> · <a href="/install/configuration/">Configuration</a></p>
</SidePage>
